  "notes": [
    "Addresses are those of the manual's tables (no 3xxxx or 4xxxx prefix), counted from 0. The manual lists the same address for registers, input registers and coils: they are different areas.",
    "32-bit values take two registers, the low word first, then the high word, and both must be written one after the other. The manual's name for each is the first register (_LO).",
    "Each register has a minimum access level: 'USUARIO' and 'ADMIN' registers need a session, opened by writing the system password in the active password register (600).",
    "The alarm statistics registers (45000 onwards, 27 blocks of 8) and the HART protocol (6.0 over 4-20 mA) are not in this map.",
    "The Modbus speed is 9600 or 19200 bps (configurable); 9600 8N1 is assumed here.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual (Spanish); not tested on a device."
  ],
